# libdl89

A small embeddable Datalog evaluation core in strict ISO C89.

`libdl89` accepts facts and rules over caller-assigned opaque identifiers and
computes the least fixed point over a caller-supplied relational store:

    eval : Program x Database -> least_fixed_point(Program, Database)

It knows nothing about syntax, symbols, SQL, persistence, transactions,
modules, provenance, negation, aggregation, side effects, or application
policy. The caller decides how programs and databases are represented,
persisted, named, reflected, mutated, and presented.

## Public API

`include/dl89.h` declares the complete surface in the `dl89_` namespace:

```c
dl89_eval_create(&config, &eval);
dl89_eval_add_fact(eval, relation, arity, tuple);
dl89_eval_add_rule(eval, &rule);
dl89_eval_run(eval);
dl89_eval_destroy(eval);
```

The relational store is the only host interface:

```c
insert(ctx, relation, arity, tuple, &inserted);
scan_open(ctx, relation, arity, values, bound, &scan);
scan_next(ctx, scan, tuple, &found);
scan_close(ctx, scan);
```

`insert` supplies set semantics and reports `inserted = 1` only for a tuple
that did not previously exist; that flag is the fixed-point primitive.
`scan_open` with `values = [a, ?, c]` and `bound = [1, 0, 1]` enumerates every
tuple `r(a, X, c)`. Arity zero is supported consistently: nullary relations
carry exactly one empty tuple.

## Semantics and contracts

- Finite monotone Datalog with fixed rule snapshots per run.
- Least fixed point; no ordering among facts carries meaning.
- Zero-body rules are facts; facts must be ground.
- Head variables must be range-restricted by the body; repeated variables
  impose equality constraints.
- Relation arity is consistent across the whole evaluator instance, covering
  both rules and `dl89_eval_add_fact`.
- `dl89_eval_add_rule` deep-copies the caller's rule; caller buffers may be
  reused or destroyed immediately.
- `dl89_eval_run` returns `DL89_EBUSY` on reentrant mutation, `DL89_ESTORE`
  on store failure, and `DL89_ENOMEM` on allocation failure. All scans opened
  by the library are closed on every return path.

## Build and test

```sh
just build        # strict C89, archive build/libdl89.a
just headers      # public header compiles standalone (GCC + Clang)
just smoke        # one end-to-end path first
just unit         # per-concern unit programs
just differential # generated programs vs. an independent reference evaluator
just stress       # bounded non-trivial workloads
just test         # smoke then unit, differential, stress
just sanitize     # whole suite under ASan+UBSan+LSan
just green        # sibling green toolchain matrix
just check        # green gate
just lint / format / doctor / clean
```

The green driver lives at `../../green/.agent/tmp/build/green` (override
`GREEN`). `.agent/` holds concept, stories, design, scenarios, and acceptance
documents; the project builds and runs without it.
